  ['The muscular contractions that move food through the digestive tract are called _____.', 'peristalsis|osmosis|ventilation|filtration', 0, 'Peristalsis pushes food forward through rhythmic contractions.'],
  ['The leaf-shaped cartilage that protects the airway during swallowing is the _____.', 'epiglottis|uvula|pylorus|villus', 0, 'The epiglottis covers the trachea during swallowing.'],
  ['The food bolus travels from the pharynx into the _____.', 'oesophagus|duodenum|colon|pancreas', 0, 'The oesophagus descends from the pharynx to the stomach.'],
  ['Liquefied food in the stomach is called _____.', 'chyme|bile|lymph|plasma', 0, 'Food liquefied during stomach digestion is called chyme.'],
  ['Chyme passes from the stomach into the duodenum through the _____ sphincter.', 'pyloric|cardiac|anal|ileal', 0, 'The pyloric sphincter controls the outlet from the stomach.'],
  ['The three parts of the small intestine are the duodenum, jejunum and _____.', 'ileum|caecum|rectum|pharynx', 0, 'The ileum is the third section of the small intestine.'],
  ['The finger-like structures that increase intestinal surface area are _____.', 'villi|alveoli|nephrons|ganglia', 0, 'Villi provide a larger surface for digestion and absorption.'],
  ['The large intestine absorbs electrolytes and _____.', 'vitamins|oxygen|bile|insulin', 0, 'Electrolytes and vitamins are listed functions of the large intestine.'],
  ['The serous membrane lining the abdominal cavity is the _____.', 'peritoneum|pleura|pericardium|meninges', 0, 'The peritoneum lines the abdominal cavity and covers abdominal organs.'],
  ['The liver produces _____.', 'bile|chyme|saliva|gastric acid', 0, 'Bile is produced by the liver.'],
  ['The gallbladder stores and _____ bile.', 'concentrates|oxygenates|filters through the lungs|turns into chyme', 0, 'The gallbladder stores and concentrates bile.'],
  ['The pancreas releases digestive enzymes as part of its _____ function.', 'exocrine|endocrine|respiratory|skeletal', 0, 'Exocrine pancreatic secretions enter the digestive tract and aid digestion.'],
  ['Insulin and glucagon help the pancreas control _____ sugar levels.', 'blood|stomach|lymph|bile', 0, 'The endocrine pancreas secretes insulin and glucagon to control blood sugar.'],
  ['Which nutrient groups are specifically identified as being chemically digested in the small intestine?', 'Carbohydrates, proteins and fats|Vitamins, minerals and water only|Oxygen, carbon dioxide and nitrogen|Bilirubin, insulin and glucagon', 0, 'The material identifies carbohydrates, proteins and fats as undergoing chemical digestion in the small intestine.'],
  ['The GI tract actively transports the flow of _____ through the whole digestive process.', 'food|blood|urine|air', 0, 'The alimentary canal actively transports food through digestion, absorption and elimination.']
